.TH "GF-ORG-UPDATE-ORG-USER-FOR-CURRENT-ORG" "1" "Apr 2026" "" ""

.SH NAME
gf-org-update-org-user-for-current-org - Updates the given user


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgf org update-org-user-for-current-org [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Updates the given user

.PP
If you are running Grafana Enterprise and have Fine-grained access control enabled you need to have a permission with action: \fBorg.users.role:update\fR with scope \fBusers:*\fR\&.

.PP
Body schema (UpdateOrgUserCommand):
{
  "role": string
}
  role                     enum: None | Viewer | Editor | Admin


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--body\fP=""
	Request body JSON or path to a JSON file (e.g. --body=/path/to/body.json, --body='{"foo": "bar"}'). The 'Body schema' block is a type reference; use --describe-body-jsonschema for a strict JSON Schema.

